# The ISO itself (and the pristine original Microsoft ISO it's built from,
# plus the intermediate extracted/mounted working files) are never committed
# here — multi-gigabyte binaries don't belong in git, GitHub hard-caps
# individual files at 100MB anyway, and redistributing Microsoft's own
# install media isn't something this repo does. Build your own from source
# with build-windows.ps1; see README.md.
*.iso
*.wim
*.esd
build/
mount/

# VM test scratch (test VHDX disks, DISM apply logs, clipboard screenshots
# from the Hyper-V boot-testing session) and root-level build run logs —
# none of this is build output that belongs in the repo.
vm/
*.log

# Local, machine-specific helper scripts (never committed): build-all.ps1 has
# hardcoded C:\Users paths, and upload-to-nextcloud.ps1 targets a private
# Nextcloud. The repo ships build-windows.ps1 as the portable build entry point.
build-all.ps1
upload-to-nextcloud.ps1
